s bigger than the 1600  so again every dollar we spend we're  saving about eighty one dollars that's  an incredibly conservative number the  actual number instead of eighty one is  probably a couple thousand because the  chances of conviction are now are much  higher than they were in the data that  we estimated from New York because the  statute of limitations are much larger  now in most states  there's many other benefits from testing  them testing these kids that we didn't  quantify so one big one is we didn't  quantify the costs associated with non  sexual crimes which are actually larger  than the costs associated with future  sexual assaults because these people on  average commit more non sexual crimes  than sexual crimes it also brings  closure to the victims it also an  interesting study people found that it  helps deter future crimes if you  actually get the kit and you put this  person into the database that once this  person finds out they're in the database  they will commit fewer future crimes  there are some people out there are just  serial sexual offenders and not just  sexual offenders but many other violent  non sexual felons and we have the  technology we have the wherewithal we  know how to get them off the street we  just haven't done it and there's an easy  way to get some of these people off the  street and we should do it  [Music]  you  [Music]

